    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d999">

                <pb facs="1123" n="1027" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1027"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to General
                            Lee.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Secretary of the Navy thinks not prudent for a vessel to remain long in Havana;
                    sanitary reasons. Should some vessel be kept there all the time? If another
                    sent, what have you to suggest as to kind of ship? Telegraph your views.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
